WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.181
Many stores sell in two places:

00:00:03.181 --> 00:00:05.009
online, and at a counter.

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:09.254
This video shows how the Point of Sale module lets your staff sell

00:00:09.254 --> 00:00:13.145
at the counter of each store, how to set up registers, how a

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:17.390
day at the till works, and how you see every shift and every sale.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.680
A store that sells online and at a counter often keeps two systems.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:32.720
Their products, prices and stock drift apart, and nobody knows what the day really sold.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.253
Cash makes it harder.

00:00:35.253 --> 00:00:41.130
Someone has to count the drawer, explain a shortage, and tell a sale from a refund.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.904
The Point of Sale module sells at the counter from a phone, a

00:00:45.904 --> 00:00:51.008
tablet or a till computer, using the same products, prices, coupons, gift cards

00:00:51.008 --> 00:00:53.230
and stock as your online store.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.710
Every counter sale is an order of your site, so it shows up

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.580
in your orders, your stock and your reports.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.938
A register is a till at one of your stores.

00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:10.710
You set up one or more at each store.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.202
A member of staff opens a shift at a register, with the cash

00:01:15.202 --> 00:01:16.790
that is in its drawer.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.379
During the shift, they ring up sales in the till app, and take

00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:22.960
cash, a card, or both.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.849
At the end of the day they count the drawer and close the shift.

00:01:27.849 --> 00:01:32.520
You see every shift, what it sold, and whether its drawer came out right.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.510
Add a location for each store under Settings, Commerce, Inventory.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:46.100
A register sells from one of them, and takes its stock from it.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.453
Give the staff who sell at the counter a role with the Sell

00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:52.171
at a register permission.

00:01:52.171 --> 00:01:55.830
Give whoever manages the stores Manage registers and shifts.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.968
The till app signs staff in with their own accounts, so every shift,

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.696
sale and cash movement says who made it.

00:02:03.696 --> 00:02:06.780
Your technical team sets that sign-in up once.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:12.022
Turn on Receipts to print and email receipts, and Stripe to take cards

00:02:12.022 --> 00:02:13.381
on a card reader.

00:02:13.381 --> 00:02:14.800
Both are optional.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.969
Open Commerce, Point of sale, Registers.

00:02:21.969 --> 00:02:26.523
Each register shows whether it is on, the address of its store, and

00:02:26.523 --> 00:02:29.080
links to its Shifts and to Edit it.

00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:30.977
Click Add register.

00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:34.647
Give it a Name that staff see when they pick a register, such

00:02:34.647 --> 00:02:39.687
as Uptown till 1, and choose its Store location, the place whose stock its sales take.

00:02:41.097 --> 00:02:43.011
Enter the Store address:

00:02:43.011 --> 00:02:47.605
the street, the city, the region, the postal code and the country.

00:02:47.605 --> 00:02:52.710
Sales at the register are taxed by this address, and its receipts show it.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.327
The country is its two-letter code.

00:02:55.816 --> 00:02:59.049
Enter the Currency its drawer holds, such as U.S.D.

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:02.396
Leave it blank to sell in the products' own currency.

00:03:02.894 --> 00:03:07.752
Under Who may sell here, tick the roles whose staff may use this register.

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:12.246
With none ticked, anyone with the Sell at a register permission can.

00:03:12.246 --> 00:03:16.436
The On switch turns the register off, so it cannot open a shift

00:03:16.436 --> 00:03:17.894
or ring up a sale.

00:03:18.389 --> 00:03:19.361
Click Save.

00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:23.252
The register is added, and staff who may sell there can open a

00:03:23.252 --> 00:03:24.969
shift from the till app.

00:03:29.169 --> 00:03:31.527
Staff sign in, and pick a register.

00:03:31.527 --> 00:03:34.805
The list shows only the registers they may sell at.

00:03:34.805 --> 00:03:37.451
They open a shift by entering the float:

00:03:37.451 --> 00:03:39.349
the cash put in the drawer.

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:43.340
They ring up a sale by adding what the buyer takes.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.207
They can look up a customer, so the sale earns points on their

00:03:47.207 --> 00:03:51.359
account, or enter a walk-in buyer's name and email for the receipt.

00:03:52.109 --> 00:03:56.549
A discount code or a gift card goes on the sale before it is paid.

00:03:57.299 --> 00:04:00.875
The buyer pays in cash, by card, or with a mix.

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:03.980
For cash, the till works out the change.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:09.109
A card is charged on the store's card terminal, or on a Stripe reader.

00:04:09.859 --> 00:04:14.519
The receipt can be printed, or emailed to the buyer when Receipts is on.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:19.058
Cash put in or taken out of the drawer outside a sale, such

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.799
as a bank run, is recorded with a reason.

00:04:22.549 --> 00:04:24.821
A return is taken at the till:

00:04:24.821 --> 00:04:28.986
the items go back on the shelf, cash is handed back from the

00:04:28.986 --> 00:04:32.079
drawer, and a card is refunded to the card.

00:04:32.829 --> 00:04:36.468
At the end of the day, staff count the drawer, add a note

00:04:36.468 --> 00:04:38.779
if it is off, and close the shift.

00:04:43.065 --> 00:04:46.005
Open Commerce, Point of sale, Shifts.

00:04:46.005 --> 00:04:51.133
It lists every shift, newest first, each Open or Closed, with when it

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.253
opened and who opened it.

00:04:53.253 --> 00:04:56.125
A closed shift shows its difference.

00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:59.895
The list in the header filters by register.

00:04:59.895 --> 00:05:05.699
Shifts, on a register in the registers list, opens the same list for that register.

00:05:06.159 --> 00:05:08.093
Click View to open a shift.

00:05:08.093 --> 00:05:12.253
It shows how many Sales it took, their Total, the Cash kept, what

00:05:12.253 --> 00:05:16.649
cards paid in Card, what gift cards paid, and what has been Refunded.

00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:21.959
Under Cash drawer, the Opening float, plus the cash put in, less the

00:05:21.959 --> 00:05:24.974
cash taken out, gives the Expected cash.

00:05:24.974 --> 00:05:29.038
Each movement is listed with its reason and who made it.

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:34.056
For a closed shift, Counted is the cash staff counted, and Difference is

00:05:34.056 --> 00:05:35.506
how far off it was.

00:05:35.506 --> 00:05:38.695
A negative difference means the drawer was short.

00:05:38.695 --> 00:05:41.653
The note given at the close is shown with it.

00:05:45.856 --> 00:05:48.848
A register sale is an order like any other.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:53.916
Open Commerce, Orders, and it is there, with a badge that names its register.

00:05:54.371 --> 00:05:57.144
The first list filters by channel:

00:05:57.144 --> 00:06:01.860
Every channel, Online, Point of sale, or Drafts sent by staff.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.981
The channel also limits the CSV export.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.456
Open a sale.

00:06:06.456 --> 00:06:10.839
Nothing is shipped, because the buyer takes the goods with them, and it

00:06:10.839 --> 00:06:13.571
was taxed by the register's store address.

00:06:14.024 --> 00:06:18.279
Its stock came off the register's store, and the sale appears in your

00:06:18.279 --> 00:06:20.434
reports by store and by channel.

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.714
A shop with an online store and a counter:

00:06:27.714 --> 00:06:31.884
one catalog and one stock, whichever way the customer buys.

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:34.098
Several stores:

00:06:34.098 --> 00:06:39.884
a register at each, selling from its own stock, with sales reported by store.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.900
A busy till with several staff:

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:48.654
every shift and every sale names who made it, and each drawer is counted and reconciled.

00:06:49.404 --> 00:06:51.580
A market stall or a pop-up:

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.864
a phone or a tablet is enough, with cash and a card reader.

00:06:57.864 --> 00:07:01.865
The Point of Sale module sells at your counters from the same store

00:07:01.865 --> 00:07:04.770
as your website, and keeps every drawer honest.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.194
Thanks for watching.

